const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"该书介绍用于评估抽样变异、偏差、覆盖率和统计精度的自助法及相关重抽样方法。 阅读时应将其放回原始样本、时点和制度环境中理解，不能把问题本身当作跨市场结论。",en:"The book explains bootstrap and related resampling methods for assessing sampling variation, bias, coverage, and other measures of statistical accuracy. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1201/9780429246593",label:{zh:"Chapman and Hall/CRC · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Chapman and Hall/CRC · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"它是方法论参考：重抽样依照既定数据生成或抽样方案进行，不能代替对估计量和依赖结构的定义。 比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系共同构成研究合同；改变其中任一选择，可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It is a methodological reference: resamples are drawn according to a specified data-generating or sampling scheme, not a substitute for defining the estimator and dependence structure. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1201/9780429246593",label:{zh:"Chapman and Hall/CRC · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Chapman and Hall/CRC · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"需要原始观测、抽样单位、估计量、重抽样方案、随机种子、重抽样次数、依赖处理以及时间或聚类边界。 字段定义、可得时点和样本筛选必须与原研究分开记录，不能因变量同名或使用最新修订值便视为可比。",en:"A use case needs the original observations, sampling unit, estimator, resampling scheme, seed, number of resamples, handling of dependence, and any chronological or cluster boundaries. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1201/9780429246593",label:{zh:"Chapman and Hall/CRC · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Chapman and Hall/CRC · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"自助法输出描述的是重抽样假设下的不确定性，并不会验证模型、消除选择偏差或让相关金融观测独立。 它只支持来源描述的经验或理论关系，不能把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"Bootstrap output describes uncertainty under its resampling assumptions; it does not validate a model, remove selection bias, or make dependent financial observations independent. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not turn association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1201/9780429246593",label:{zh:"Chapman and Hall/CRC · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Chapman and Hall/CRC · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"声明抽样单位和估计目标；保留随机种子和次数；在需要时采用区块或聚类结构；保持训练、验证和测试期间隔离。 开展后续分析前，应将这些选择写入版本化研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Declare the sampling unit and estimand; preserve random seed and resample count; choose block or cluster structure where needed; and keep training, validation, and test periods separate. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1201/9780429246593",label:{zh:"Chapman and Hall/CRC · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Chapman and Hall/CRC · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Chapman and Hall/CRC · DOI record。重抽样不能恢复原始样本不存在的信息，也不能使超出既定抽样设计的因果或预测主张成立。 如需数值结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Chapman and Hall/CRC · DOI record. Resampling cannot recover information absent from the original sample or justify causal and predictive claims beyond the stated sampling design. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1201/9780429246593",label:{zh:"Chapman and Hall/CRC · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Chapman and Hall/CRC · DOI record · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“An Introduction to the Bootstrap”公开说明的研究对象、设计与适用边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。重抽样不能恢复原始样本不存在的信息，也不能使超出既定抽样设计的因果或预测主张成立。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “An Introduction to the Bootstrap”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
